  "id": "Compound::DB01594 - Gene::2561",
  "verbalization": "Cinolazepam is shown to bind to Gabrr3 and Gabrp, both of which are involved in the Gaba-a receptor activity, which is ultimately associated with Gabrb2. The evidence suggests that Cinolazepam may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the Gaba-a receptor complex, with Gabrb2 being a key component of this pathway. The high scores in the final_score indicate a strong and consistent relationship between Cinolazepam and Gabrb2, supported by multiple binding and functional interactions. The overlapping roles of Gabrr3 and Gabrp in the Gaba-a receptor activity suggest that Cinolazepam may modulate the function of the Gaba-a receptor complex, potentially influencing neuronal signaling. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cinolazepam and Gabrb2, though further studies are needed to confirm the specific molecular interactions and therapeutic implications.",
